WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.830
A government wants to protect
its farmers from cheaper

2
00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:04.930
food arriving from abroad.

3
00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:06.440
It has a toolbox.

4
00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.200
A tax on imports.

5
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.260
A limit on how much comes in.

6
00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:12.410
A payment to its own farmers.

7
00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:16.190
A ban. Or piles of border paperwork.

8
00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:18.970
Each tool shields the farmers differently.

9
00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:21.720
Start with the tax, called a tariff.

10
00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.360
So when a country taxes goods from abroad,

11
00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.240
who ends up paying, and
who comes out ahead?

12
00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:31.070
In this mission, you'll build the
tariff diagram frame by frame,

13
00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:33.900
and track where every slice of value goes.

14
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.520
Then you'll set a tariff
yourself and predict what

15
00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:39.130
happens to the money
the government collects.

16
00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:43.390
Your mission: find out who really
pays when imports are taxed.
